Make the Xwayland socket directory overridable and the abstract-namespace bind optional.

Android has no writable /tmp and MatonOS runs the compositor inside an app
process, so the hardcoded /tmp/.X11-unix paths cannot be used. Honor
WLR_XWAYLAND_SOCKET_DIR for both the socket directory and the lock file
(inside the directory; the default stays /tmp/.X11-unix). Honor
WLR_XWAYLAND_NO_ABSTRACT=1 to skip the abstract-namespace bind: abstract
sockets have no filesystem permissions, so per-display servers can then
isolate clients through filesystem socket ownership alone. Server startup,
argv construction and teardown handle a missing first listen fd.
